        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: accusare",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "accusare — \"to accuse\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Mi accusano di aver preso i soldi, ma non è vero. They accuse me of taking the money, but it is not true."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Accusare qualcuno di qualcosa. Accusare un dolore — to feel a pain."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "accusare is inherited from Latin accūsāre \"to call to account, to accuse\" (EtymDB), built from ad \"to\" and causa \"a case, a lawsuit\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
